Undo: "Five Minutes" (film made in code, NEAR HACKATHON 2026)

Picture
- three.js r170 (MIT), rendered headless; post-processing from the Lemo-Opuscar library's core/three/post.js
- Fonts: Archivo (SIL Open Font License 1.1, fonts/OFL-Archivo.txt), JetBrains Mono (SIL OFL 1.1, fonts/OFL-JetBrainsMono.txt), the same fonts as the Undo site
- img/frost.webp, img/stage-wide.webp, img/cassette-960.webp: the Undo site's own assets (undo/app/public/undo/)
- Everything shown on the phone is redrawn from the live app (undo-cyan.vercel.app) and real NEAR testnet transactions (see TREATMENT.md, CLAIMS.md)

Sound
- Voices: Kokoro-82M text-to-speech (Apache License 2.0), voices bm_lewis and am_onyx
- Instruments: Versilian Community Sample Library, VCSL (CC0 1.0): tubular bells, bowed vibraphone, glockenspiel, marimba, gran cassa, gong, suspended cymbal, clash cymbals, toms, frame drum, hand chimes, woodblock
- Synth bass, pads, sweeps and foley synthesised in code (numpy)

Inspiration (grammar only, nothing copied): battle-anime guardian spirits, time-stop and rewind scenes.
